To implement this cleanly, we will establish a robust **Material 3 Token System** with **high-luminance fallback tokens** for dark theme compliance. 

Here is the technical specification and implementation plan for the `UserSettingsView` refactor.

---

# Specification: `UserSettingsView` Material 3 Refactor & Dark Theme

## 1. Color Token Architecture (with Fallback Strategy)
When the brand color (e.g., a deep brand blue `#003366`) has low luminance, using it directly in dark mode violates WCAG 4.5:1. We define a **high-luminance fallback token** (`--md-sys-color-primary-fallback` or Tone 80) for interactive elements and text, while reserving the raw brand color only for large non-functional backgrounds or decorative elements.

### Token Map (`_tokens.scss`)

```scss
// src/styles/_tokens.scss

:root {
  // --- SPACING TOKENS (M3 Compact/Standard) ---
  --md-sys-spacing-xs: 4px;
  --md-sys-spacing-sm: 8px;
  --md-sys-spacing-md: 16px;
  --md-sys-spacing-lg: 24px;
  --md-sys-spacing-xl: 32px;

  // --- SHAPE TOKENS ---
  --md-sys-shape-corner-small: 8px;
  --md-sys-shape-corner-medium: 12px;
  --md-sys-shape-corner-large: 16px;

  // --- LIGHT THEME TOKENS (Default) ---
  --md-sys-color-background: #FBFDF7;
  --md-sys-color-on-background: #1A1C18;
  --md-sys-color-surface: #FBFDF7;
  --md-sys-color-surface-variant: #E0E4D6;
  --md-sys-color-on-surface: #1A1C18;
  --md-sys-color-on-surface-variant: #43483E;
  --md-sys-color-outline: #74796E;

  // Brand Color (Low Luminance)
  --brand-color-raw: #003366; 

  // Interactive Primary (Light Theme uses raw brand color as it has high contrast against light BG)
  --md-sys-color-primary: var(--brand-color-raw);
  --md-sys-color-on-primary: #FFFFFF;
  --md-sys-color-primary-container: #D2E4FF;
  --md-sys-color-on-primary-container: #001D3D;
}

[data-theme="dark"] {
  // --- DARK THEME TOKENS ---
  --md-sys-color-background: #1A1C18;
  --md-sys-color-on-background: #E3E3DC;
  --md-sys-color-surface: #121411;
  --md-sys-color-surface-variant: #43483E;
  --md-sys-color-on-surface: #E3E3DC;
  --md-sys-color-on-surface-variant: #C4C8BA;
  --md-sys-color-outline: #8E9285;

  // Brand Color remains raw for brand-specific non-functional elements
  --brand-color-raw: #003366; 

  // FALLBACK HIGH-LUMINANCE TOKENS FOR WCAG COMPLIANCE
  // Instead of raw brand color, we use Tone 80 (high-luminance blue-gray/light-blue)
  // This guarantees 4.5:1 contrast against --md-sys-color-surface (#121411)
  --md-sys-color-primary: #A5C8FF; // Fallback High-Luminance Token
  --md-sys-color-on-primary: #00315E;
  --md-sys-color-primary-container: #004785;
  --md-sys-color-on-primary-container: #D2E4FF;
}
```

---

## 2. Layout Refactoring Strategy for `UserSettingsView`
The `UserSettingsView` layout will be refactored to use CSS Grid and Flexbox driven entirely by M3 spacing and color tokens.

### Key Layout Sections:
1. **Navigation/Sidebar**:
   - Background: `--md-sys-color-surface`
   - Active Item: `--md-sys-color-primary-container` with text `--md-sys-color-on-primary-container`
   - Border/Divider: `--md-sys-color-outline` (subtle)
2. **Settings Cards/Panels**:
   - Background: `--md-sys-color-surface-variant` or elevated surface
   - Border Radius: `--md-sys-shape-corner-medium`
   - Padding: `--md-sys-spacing-lg`
3. **Form Controls & Inputs**:
   - Borders: `--md-sys-color-outline`
   - Focus State: `--md-sys-color-primary` (using the high-luminance fallback in dark mode)
   - Text: `--md-sys-color-on-surface`

---

## 3. SCSS Implementation Pattern

We will structure the component SCSS using defensive, scoped selectors:

```scss
// src/components/UserSettingsView/UserSettingsView.scss
@import '../../styles/tokens';

.user-settings-container {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 280px 1fr;
  gap: var(--md-sys-spacing-lg);
  padding: var(--md-sys-spacing-xl);
  background-color: var(--md-sys-color-background);
  color: var(--md-sys-color-on-background);
  min-height: 100vh;
  transition: background-color 0.3s ease, color 0.3s ease;

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    padding: var(--md-sys-spacing-md);
  }
}

.settings-sidebar {
  background-color: var(--md-sys-color-surface);
  border-right: 1px solid var(--md-sys-color-outline);
  padding: var(--md-sys-spacing-md);

  .nav-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: var(--md-sys-spacing-sm) var(--md-sys-spacing-md);
    border-radius: var(--md-sys-shape-corner-small);
    color: var(--md-sys-color-on-surface-variant);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: background-color 0.2s ease;

    &:hover {
      background-color: var(--md-sys-color-surface-variant);
    }

    &.active {
      // Uses high-luminance fallback primary container in dark mode
      background-color: var(--md-sys-color-primary-container);
      color: var(--md-sys-color-on-primary-container);
      font-weight: 600;
    }
  }
}

.settings-content {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: var(--md-sys-spacing-lg);
}

.settings-card {
  background-color: var(--md-sys-color-surface);
  border: 1px solid var(--md-sys-color-outline);
  border-radius: var(--md-sys-shape-corner-medium);
  padding: var(--md-sys-spacing-lg);

  .card-title {
    color: var(--md-sys-color-on-surface);
    margin-bottom: var(--md-sys-spacing-sm);
  }

  .card-description {
    color: var(--md-sys-color-on-surface-variant);
    margin-bottom: var(--md-sys-spacing-md);
  }
}
```

---

## 4. Verification & Testing Plan
1. **Contrast Ratio Audit**: Use automated tools (or manual calculation) to verify that all text elements on `--md-sys-color-background` and `--md-sys-color-surface` have a contrast ratio of at least **4.5:1** in both light and dark modes.
2. **Theme Toggle Test**: Ensure smooth transition when the `data-theme="dark"` attribute is toggled on the `<html>` or `<body>` element.
3. **Responsive Layout Test**: Verify that the grid collapses gracefully to a single column on mobile viewports (< 768px).

